Z||000001||terryk||08-06-2000||10:22 PM||||I've done a 3800 SC swap into a Ciera GT and I'm in the middle of a 3.4L DOHC swap into my 86 Fiero.<P>Fiqure about 40 hours to go through the harnesses and combine and wrap them up. It's easier to do with the engine installed and the old harness. Then you can routine each wire to the ECM, power connector, or accessory connector and make them clean.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||08-06-2000||10:28 PM||||Lets see at $50 an hour thats $2000 for your time.  I have heard that the wiring of the 3800 is a real pain.  ACE makes some harnesses for the conversion also.<P>Pat youself on the back terryk, thats one job I would not even think of tackeling.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||08-07-2000||12:26 AM||||Thanks, it wasn't that bad. It just takes time. Once the engine is installed, you're pretty motivated to get the wiring done.||||reg||7
